-- ccc27-s737-1-restitution.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 737.1 to 741.2 (restitution).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.
-- Section 738(2) (a regulation-making power of the lieutenant governor in council) and section 739.4(2) (a designation power) are machinery: see NOTES.md, coverage.

§ `Sections 737.1 to 741.2 -- Restitution`

§§ `737.1 Court to consider restitution order`

-- src:15808 | 737.1 (1) If an offender is convicted or is discharged under section 730 of an offence, the court that sentences or discharges the offender, in addition to any other measure imposed on the offender, shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739.
@ref s 737.1(1) (src:15808)
GIVEN convicted IS A BOOLEAN
      `discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(1) the court shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739` MEANS
    IF convicted OR `discharged under section 730`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offender is convicted or is discharged under section 730 of an offence" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)

-- src:15810 | (2) As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing the sentence, the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to provide the victims with an opportunity to indicate whether they are seeking restitution for their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable.
@ref s 737.1(2) (src:15810)
GIVEN `there has been a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(2) the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to give the victims an opportunity to indicate whether they are seeking restitution` MEANS
    IF `there has been a finding of guilt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt" (a duty whose "after" is unmet, fork F-3)

-- The time limit in the same sentence: "in any event before imposing the sentence". Dates carry no time of day, so the same day is not decided.
-- src:15810 | (2) As soon as feasible after a finding of guilt and in any event before imposing the sentence, the court shall inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps have been taken to provide the victims with an opportunity to indicate whether they are seeking restitution for their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable.
@ref s 737.1(2) (src:15810)
GIVEN `the day of the inquiry` IS A DATE
      `the day the sentence was imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(2) the court has made the inquiry before imposing the sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day of the inquiry` LESS THAN `the day the sentence was imposed` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day of the inquiry` EQUALS `the day the sentence was imposed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): which came first on the same day is not recorded by a date
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event before imposing the sentence"

-- src:15812 | (3) On application of the prosecutor or on its own motion, the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victims to indicate whether they are seeking restitution or to establish their losses and damages, if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 737.1(3) (src:15812)
GIVEN `on application of the prosecutor or on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings to permit the victims to indicate whether they are seeking restitution or to establish their losses and damages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`on application of the prosecutor or on its own motion`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application of the prosecutor or on its own motion" (an "on" gate, treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed in the fork register, group (i))
        IF `the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere with the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that the adjournment would not interfere" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

DECLARE `s 737.1(4) method of indicating` IS ONE OF
    `s 737.1(4) completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII`
    `s 737.1(4) completing a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction`
    `s 737.1(4) using another method approved by the court`
    `s 737.1(4) using a method that none of those approves`

-- src:15814 | (4) Victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII or a form approved for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction or by using any other method approved by the court, and, if they are seeking restitution, shall establish their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable, in the same manner.
@ref s 737.1(4) (src:15814)
GIVEN method IS A `s 737.1(4) method of indicating`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(4) victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by the method` MEANS
    CONSIDER method
    WHEN `s 737.1(4) completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 737.1(4) completing a form approved by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 737.1(4) using another method approved by the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 737.1(4) using a method that none of those approves` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or by using any other method approved by the court"

-- Section 737.1 is one of the sections for which section 2.2 lets an individual act on the victim's behalf; the answer is taken as an input and passed on unchanged.
-- src:15814 | (4) Victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII or a form approved for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction or by using any other method approved by the court, and, if they are seeking restitution, shall establish their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable, in the same manner.
@ref s 737.1(4) (src:15814)
GIVEN `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(4) the individual indicates on the victim's behalf, by s 2.2` MEANS
    `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)`

-- src:15814 | (4) Victims and other persons may indicate whether they are seeking restitution by completing Form 34.1 in Part XXVIII or a form approved for that purpose by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the court is exercising its jurisdiction or by using any other method approved by the court, and, if they are seeking restitution, shall establish their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable, in the same manner.
@ref s 737.1(4) (src:15814)
GIVEN `the person is seeking restitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the losses and damages is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the losses and damages are established in the same manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(4) the person seeking restitution has met the requirement to establish readily ascertainable losses and damages` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is seeking restitution`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if they are seeking restitution, shall establish" (the requirement does not arise; fork F-3)
        IF `the amount of the losses and damages is readily ascertainable` AND `the losses and damages are established in the same manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall establish their losses and damages, the amount of which must be readily ascertainable, in the same manner"

-- src:15816 | (5) If a victim seeks restitution and the court does not make a restitution order, it shall include in the record a statement of the court’s reasons for not doing so.
@ref s 737.1(5) (src:15816)
GIVEN `a victim seeks restitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court does not make a restitution order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737.1(5) the court shall include in the record a statement of its reasons for not making a restitution order` MEANS
    IF `a victim seeks restitution` AND `the court does not make a restitution order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a victim seeks restitution and the court does not make a restitution order" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)

§§ `738 Restitution to victims of offences`

-- src:15818 | 738 (1) Where an offender is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence, the court imposing sentence on or discharging the offender may, on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion, in addition to any other measure imposed on the offender, order that the offender make restitution to another person as follows:
@ref s 738(1) (src:15818)
GIVEN convicted IS A BOOLEAN
      `discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (convicted OR `discharged under section 730`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence" (a "where" gate, ruling (b); listed in the fork register, group (i))
        IF NOT (`on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the Attorney General or on its own motion" (an "on" gate, treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed in the fork register, group (i))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The five heads of restitution each fix a ceiling. A ceiling is a number, so "not covered" is NOTHING (a NUMBER has no FALSE).
-- src:15819 | (a) in the case of damage to, or the loss or destruction of, the property of any person as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender, by paying to the person an amount not exceeding the replacement value of the property as of the date the order is imposed, less the value of any part of the property that is returned to that person as of the date it is returned, where the amount is readily ascertainable;
@ref s 738(1)(a) (src:15819)
GIVEN `the damage, loss or destruction is a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the replacement value of the property as of the date the order is imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any part of the property that is returned to that person as of the date it is returned` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` MEANS
    IF `the damage, loss or destruction is a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender` AND `the amount is readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST (max 0 (`the replacement value of the property as of the date the order is imposed` MINUS `the value of any part of the property that is returned to that person as of the date it is returned`))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the amount is readily ascertainable" (a ceiling is a number, so no FALSE is available; fork F-4)

-- src:15820 | (b) in the case of bodily or psychological harm to any person as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender, by paying to the person an amount not exceeding all pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, including loss of income or support, if the amount is readily ascertainable;
@ref s 738(1)(b) (src:15820)
GIVEN `the harm is bodily or psychological harm to a person as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, including loss of income or support` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 738(1)(b) the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` MEANS
    IF `the harm is bodily or psychological harm to a person as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender` AND `the amount is readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST `all pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, including loss of income or support`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the amount is readily ascertainable" (fork F-4)

-- src:15821 | (c) in the case of bodily or psychological harm or threat of such harm to the offender’s intimate partner or child, or any other person, as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender, where the intimate partner, child or other person was a member of the offender’s household at the relevant time, by paying to the person in question, independently of any amount ordered to be paid under paragraphs (a) and (b), an amount of not more than the actual and reasonable expenses incurred by that person, as a result of moving out of the offender’s household, for temporary housing, food, child care and transportation, where the amount is readily ascertainable;
@ref s 738(1)(c) (src:15821)
GIVEN `there was bodily or psychological harm, or a threat of such harm, to the offender's intimate partner or child, or any other person, as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a member of the offender's household at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the actual and reasonable expenses incurred as a result of moving out of the offender's household, for temporary housing, food, child care and transportation` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` MEANS
    IF `there was bodily or psychological harm, or a threat of such harm, to the offender's intimate partner or child, or any other person, as a result of the commission of the offence or the arrest or attempted arrest of the offender`
       AND `the person was a member of the offender's household at the relevant time`
       AND `the amount is readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST `the actual and reasonable expenses incurred as a result of moving out of the offender's household, for temporary housing, food, child care and transportation`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the intimate partner, child or other person was a member of the offender's household at the relevant time" and "where the amount is readily ascertainable" (fork F-4)

-- src:15822 | (d) in the case of an offence under section 402.2 or 403, by paying to a person who, as a result of the offence, incurs expenses to re-establish their identity, including expenses to replace their identity documents and to correct their credit history and credit rating, an amount that is not more than the amount of those expenses, to the extent that they are reasonable, if the amount is readily ascertainable; and
@ref s 738(1)(d) (src:15822)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person incurs expenses to re-establish their identity as a result of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of those expenses that is reasonable` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` MEANS
    IF elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 402.2, 403) AND `the person incurs expenses to re-establish their identity as a result of the offence` AND `the amount is readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST `the part of those expenses that is reasonable`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an offence under section 402.2 or 403" and "if the amount is readily ascertainable" (fork F-4)

-- src:15823 | (e) in the case of an offence under subsection 162.1(1), by paying to a person who, as a result of the offence, incurs expenses to remove the intimate image from the Internet or other digital network, an amount that is not more than the amount of those expenses, to the extent that they are reasonable, if the amount is readily ascertainable.
@ref s 738(1)(e) (src:15823)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person incurs expenses to remove the intimate image from the Internet or other digital network as a result of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of those expenses that is reasonable` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 738(1)(e) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing the intimate image` MEANS
    IF offence's `section` EQUALS 162.1 AND offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
       AND `the person incurs expenses to remove the intimate image from the Internet or other digital network as a result of the offence`
       AND `the amount is readily ascertainable`
    THEN JUST `the part of those expenses that is reasonable`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an offence under subsection 162.1(1)" and "if the amount is readily ascertainable" (fork F-4)

§§ `739 to 739.4 Restitution to persons acting in good faith; ability to pay; payment; more than one person; public authority`

DECLARE `s 739 head` IS ONE OF
    `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice`
    `s 739(b) a person from whom the offender borrowed money on the security of that property, acting in good faith and without notice`

-- src:15827 | 739 Where an offender is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence and
-- src:15828 | (a) any property obtained as a result of the commission of the offence has been conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration to a person acting in good faith and without notice, or
-- src:15829 | (b) the offender has borrowed money on the security of that property from a person acting in good faith and without notice,
-- src:15830 | the court may, where that property has been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession of that property at the time the offence was committed, order the offender to pay as restitution to the person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) an amount not exceeding the amount of consideration for that property or the total amount outstanding in respect of the loan, as the case may be.
@ref s 739 (src:15827-15830)
GIVEN convicted IS A BOOLEAN
      `discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      head IS A `s 739 head`
      `the property has been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession at the time the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (convicted OR `discharged under section 730`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender is convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence" (a "where" gate, ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF NOT (`the property has been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession at the time the offence was committed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that property has been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession" (a "where" gate, ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the head is paragraph (a) or (b): both name a person to whom restitution may be ordered

-- src:15830 | the court may, where that property has been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession of that property at the time the offence was committed, order the offender to pay as restitution to the person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) an amount not exceeding the amount of consideration for that property or the total amount outstanding in respect of the loan, as the case may be.
@ref s 739 (src:15830)
GIVEN head IS A `s 739 head`
      `the amount of consideration for that property` IS A NUMBER
      `the total amount outstanding in respect of the loan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 739 the ceiling on restitution to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER head
    WHEN `s 739(a) a person to whom property obtained by the offence was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, acting in good faith and without notice` THEN `the amount of consideration for that property`
    WHEN `s 739(b) a person from whom the offender borrowed money on the security of that property, acting in good faith and without notice` THEN `the total amount outstanding in respect of the loan`

-- src:15832 | 739.1 The offender’s financial means or ability to pay does not prevent the court from making an order under section 738 or 739.
@ref s 739.1 (src:15832)
GIVEN `the ground relied on is the offender's financial means or ability to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739.1 the offender's financial means or ability to pay prevents the court from making an order under section 738 or 739` MEANS
    IF `the ground relied on is the offender's financial means or ability to pay`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prevent the court from making an order under section 738 or 739"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section speaks only of financial means and ability to pay

DECLARE `s 739.2 term of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 739.2 payment of the full amount specified in the order by the day specified in the order`
    `s 739.2 payment in instalments under a periodic payment scheme set out in the order`

-- src:15834 | 739.2 In making an order under section 738 or 739, the court shall require the offender to pay the full amount specified in the order by the day specified in the order, unless the court is of the opinion that the amount should be paid in instalments, in which case the court shall set out a periodic payment scheme in the order.
@ref s 739.2 (src:15834)
GIVEN `the court is of the opinion that the amount should be paid in instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 739.2 term of payment`
`s 739.2 the term of payment the court shall require in the order` MEANS
    IF `the court is of the opinion that the amount should be paid in instalments`
    THEN `s 739.2 payment in instalments under a periodic payment scheme set out in the order`
    ELSE `s 739.2 payment of the full amount specified in the order by the day specified in the order`

-- src:15836 | 739.3 An order under section 738 or 739 may be made in respect of more than one person, in which case the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person. The order may also specify the order of priority in which those persons are to be paid.
@ref s 739.3 (src:15836)
GIVEN `the order is made in respect of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739.3 the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person` MEANS
    IF `the order is made in respect of more than one person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person" (the case is an order in respect of more than one person; fork F-3)

-- src:15836 | 739.3 An order under section 738 or 739 may be made in respect of more than one person, in which case the order must specify the amount that is payable to each person. The order may also specify the order of priority in which those persons are to be paid.
@ref s 739.3 (src:15836)
GIVEN `the order is made in respect of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739.3 the order may specify the order of priority in which those persons are to be paid` MEANS
    IF `the order is made in respect of more than one person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "those persons" presupposes more than one person

-- src:15838 | 739.4 (1) On the request of a person in whose favour an order under section 738 or 739 would be made, the court may make the order in favour of a public authority, designated by the regulations, who is to be responsible for enforcing the order and remitting to the person making the request all amounts received under it.
@ref s 739.4(1) (src:15838)
GIVEN `a person in whose favour an order under section 738 or 739 would be made has made the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is a public authority designated by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 739.4(1) the court may make the order in favour of a public authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a person in whose favour an order under section 738 or 739 would be made has made the request`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the request of a person in whose favour an order under section 738 or 739 would be made" (an "on" gate, treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `the authority is a public authority designated by the regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a public authority, designated by the regulations" (who is designated is outside the sources)

§§ `740 to 741.2 Priority; deemed restitution orders; enforcement; notice; civil remedy`

-- src:15842 | 740 Where the court finds it applicable and appropriate in the circumstances of a case to make, in relation to an offender, an order of restitution under section 738 or 739, and
-- src:15843 | (a) an order of forfeiture under this or any other Act of Parliament may be made in respect of property that is the same as property in respect of which the order of restitution may be made, or
-- src:15844 | (b) the court is considering ordering the offender to pay a fine and it appears to the court that the offender would not have the means or ability to comply with both the order of restitution and the order to pay the fine,
-- src:15845 | the court shall first make the order of restitution and shall then consider whether and to what extent an order of forfeiture or an order to pay a fine is appropriate in the circumstances.
@ref s 740 (src:15842-15845)
GIVEN `the court finds it applicable and appropriate in the circumstances to make an order of restitution under section 738 or 739` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order of forfeiture may be made in respect of property that is the same as property in respect of which the order of restitution may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is considering ordering the offender to pay a fine and it appears the offender would not have the means or ability to comply with both orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` MEANS
    IF `the court finds it applicable and appropriate in the circumstances to make an order of restitution under section 738 or 739`
       AND (`an order of forfeiture may be made in respect of property that is the same as property in respect of which the order of restitution may be made`
            OR `the court is considering ordering the offender to pay a fine and it appears the offender would not have the means or ability to comply with both orders`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court finds it applicable and appropriate ... and (a) ... or (b) ..." (a "where" gate on a duty, ruling (b)) (fork F-3)

DECLARE `s 740.1 order` IS ONE OF
    `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 732.1`
    `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 742.3`
    `s 740.1 an order of another kind`

-- src:15847 | 740.1 If an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3 contains a requirement for payment and the order terminates before all required payments are made, the portion of the order that relates to that requirement is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739, as the case may be. The restitution order remains in force until all the required payments are made.
@ref s 740.1 (src:15847)
GIVEN order IS A `s 740.1 order`
      `the order contains a requirement for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order terminates before all required payments are made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 740.1 the portion of the order that relates to the requirement for payment is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `s 740.1 an order of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3"
    WHEN `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 732.1` THEN `s 740.1 the two facts`
    WHEN `s 740.1 an order referred to in section 742.3` THEN `s 740.1 the two facts`
    WHERE
        `s 740.1 the two facts` MEANS
            IF `the order contains a requirement for payment` AND `the order terminates before all required payments are made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order ... contains a requirement for payment and the order terminates before all required payments are made"

-- src:15847 | 740.1 If an order referred to in section 732.1 or 742.3 contains a requirement for payment and the order terminates before all required payments are made, the portion of the order that relates to that requirement is deemed to continue as a restitution order made under section 738 or 739, as the case may be. The restitution order remains in force until all the required payments are made.
@ref s 740.1 (src:15847)
GIVEN `the deemed restitution order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the required payments are made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 740.1 the restitution order remains in force` MEANS
    IF `the deemed restitution order is in force` AND NOT (`all the required payments are made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "remains in force until all the required payments are made"

DECLARE `s 741(1) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 741(1) an order under section 732.1`
    `s 741(1) an order under section 738`
    `s 741(1) an order under section 739`
    `s 741(1) an order under section 742.3`
    `s 741(1) an order of another kind`

-- src:15849 | 741 (1) An offender who fails to pay all of the amount that is ordered to be paid under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3 by the day specified in the order or who fails to make a periodic payment required under the order is in default of the order and the person to whom the amount, or the periodic payment, as the case may be, was to be made may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment any amount ordered to be paid that remains unpaid under the order in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount, and that judgment is enforceable against the offender in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref s 741(1) (src:15849)
GIVEN order IS A `s 741(1) order`
      `the offender fails to pay all of the amount ordered to be paid by the day specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender fails to make a periodic payment required under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF order EQUALS `s 741(1) an order of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ordered to be paid under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3"
        IF `the offender fails to pay all of the amount ordered to be paid by the day specified in the order` OR `the offender fails to make a periodic payment required under the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offender who fails to pay all of the amount ... or who fails to make a periodic payment ... is in default" (a failed relative clause read as the text's no: fork F-7)

-- src:15849 | 741 (1) An offender who fails to pay all of the amount that is ordered to be paid under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3 by the day specified in the order or who fails to make a periodic payment required under the order is in default of the order and the person to whom the amount, or the periodic payment, as the case may be, was to be made may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment any amount ordered to be paid that remains unpaid under the order in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount, and that judgment is enforceable against the offender in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref s 741(1) (src:15849)
GIVEN `the offender is in default, by s 741(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is a civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` MEANS
    IF `the offender is in default, by s 741(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the order is filed` AND `the court is a civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who fails ... is in default of the order and the person ... may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment ... in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:15849 | 741 (1) An offender who fails to pay all of the amount that is ordered to be paid under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3 by the day specified in the order or who fails to make a periodic payment required under the order is in default of the order and the person to whom the amount, or the periodic payment, as the case may be, was to be made may, by filing the order, enter as a judgment any amount ordered to be paid that remains unpaid under the order in any civil court in Canada that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount, and that judgment is enforceable against the offender in the same manner as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in that court in civil proceedings.
@ref s 741(1) (src:15849)
GIVEN `a judgment is entered under subsection 741(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(1) the judgment is enforceable against the offender as if it were a judgment rendered against the offender in civil proceedings` MEANS
    IF `a judgment is entered under subsection 741(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that judgment"

-- src:15851 | (2) All or any part of an amount that is ordered to be paid under section 738 or 739 may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender if the court making the order, on being satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender, so directs.
@ref s 741(2) (src:15851)
GIVEN `the amount is ordered to be paid under section 738 or 739` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741(2) all or any part of the amount may be taken out of moneys found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest` MEANS
    IF `the amount is ordered to be paid under section 738 or 739`
       AND `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender`
       AND `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender`
       AND `the court so directs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court making the order, on being satisfied that ownership ... is not disputed ..., so directs" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

DECLARE `s 741.1 recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 741.1 the person to whom the restitution is ordered to be paid`
    `s 741.1 the public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2)`
    `s 741.1 the person to whom the public authority is to remit amounts received under the order`

-- src:15853 | 741.1 If a court makes an order of restitution under section 738 or 739, it shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the person to whom the restitution is ordered to be paid, and if it is to be paid to a public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2), to the public authority and the person to whom the public authority is to remit amounts received under the order.
@ref s 741.1 (src:15853)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 741.1 recipient`
      `the court makes an order of restitution under section 738 or 739` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restitution is to be paid to a public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741.1 the court shall cause notice of the content of the order, or a copy of the order, to be given to the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the court makes an order of restitution under section 738 or 739`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court makes an order of restitution under section 738 or 739" (a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 741.1 the person to whom the restitution is ordered to be paid` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the restitution is to be paid to a public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is to be paid to a public authority designated by regulations made under subsection 739.4(2), to the public authority and the person to whom the public authority is to remit"

-- src:15855 | 741.2 A civil remedy for an act or omission is not affected by reason only that an order for restitution under section 738 or 739 has been made in respect of that act or omission.
@ref s 741.2 (src:15855)
GIVEN `the only reason relied on is that an order for restitution under section 738 or 739 has been made in respect of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 741.2 a civil remedy for an act or omission is affected by the restitution order` MEANS
    IF `the only reason relied on is that an order for restitution under section 738 or 739 has been made in respect of the act or omission`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A civil remedy for an act or omission is not affected by reason only that an order for restitution under section 738 or 739 has been made"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only"
